A||||4||Howard_Sacks||Offset confusion||||1||
Z||000000||Howard_Sacks||12-06-2001||06:56 PM||||Um, maybe I'm missing something but I thought that the bigger the offset, the more the wheel should stick out the side of the car.  I was told if I run 50mm offset rims that they would stick out about 1cm.<P>How come when I put 35mm offset fiero rims on my subaru(that's supposed to use the 50mm offset) they stuck out?  <P>Fiero Rim:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.howard.saturnet.net/leggy/35mmoffset.jpg"> <BR>Factory Rim:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.howard.saturnet.net/leggy/factoryoffset.jpg"> <P>Why do I care?  I want to run the same set of autocross tires on both cars.<P>btw, don't buy RE92s if you do aggressive driving:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.howard.saturnet.net/leggy/morewear.jpg"> <BR>those are only one year old!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||88-DOHC||12-06-2001||07:48 PM||||No, the bigger the offset, the more they tuck in. Think of it as the distance from the center of the wheel, to the wheel backing plate (where the lugs poke through). The greater that distance, the more you wheel tucks under the car, the less that distance, the more they would stick out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-06-2001||08:46 PM||||depends, some companies use rear offset for measuring, some use front. makes a huge difference. some also dont even call it offset, they prefer 'Back spacing'.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||12-06-2001||08:59 PM||||Depends on if you're talking positive or negative offset.  Old rear wheel drive cars used positive offset or "deep-dish" wheels when going with larger widths, and the more offset, the more they stuck out.  On most FWD, and the Fiero, they use negative offset, so the more negative offset you have, the more tucked in they will be.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com</A>  has a great explanation of offset and what it is, complete with diagrams.  Check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Howard_Sacks||12-07-2001||02:56 PM||||Ok thanks for the replies, I was just making sure that I'm not going crazy.  It's a good thing I didn't buy 50mm offset rims.  I would have been PO'd when I lost an inch of track! and I have an extra set of Fiero rims.<P>You guys don't think I'm going to break a hub or anything on the subaru with the smaller offset rim?  Also, they don't stick out enough to upset "the law" right?||||reg||14
